BT /F2 18 Tf 54 738 Td (Datadog for Claude Cowork. Observability by) Tj ET
BT /F2 18 Tf 54 714 Td (conversation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 678 Td (Audience: Platform and SRE engineers) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 662 Td (Decision: Pilot the Datadog connector with one team, keep Datadog permissions scoped,) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 646 Td (and treat the Preview status as a rollout risk.) Tj ET
BT /F2 14 Tf 54 616 Td (Executive Summary) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 597 Td (The Datadog plugin and connector let Claude query Datadog logs, metrics, traces,) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 581 Td (dashboards and monitors through the Datadog MCP Server.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 54 555 Td (Narration) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 538 Td (Datadog for Claude Cowork. Your telemetry, one question away. Here is what the plugin) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 522 Td (does, how it connects, and where a team should be careful.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 501 Td (The Datadog Model Context Protocol server bridges your observability data to agents.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 485 Td (Logs, metrics, traces, dashboards, and monitors become things you can simply ask about.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 464 Td (For Claude, including Cowork, the official connector is the recommended path, and it) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 448 Td (adds in-product visualizations. Claude Code installs the same server as a plugin from) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 432 Td (the official marketplace.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 411 Td (Setup is short. Choose your Datadog site, then sign in with OAuth in the browser. Keys) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 395 Td (are an alternative, and any older manual server or custom connector should be removed) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 379 Td (first.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 358 Td (Access is not widened. You still need the Datadog permissions for the data you query,) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 342 Td (and the plugin states that no Datadog credentials are sent to the model provider.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 321 Td (Tool groups can be switched on or off, so a team can expose only the products it needs.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 305 Td (Start with one narrow toolset.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 284 Td (Treat the preview label as a rollout risk. The server is HIPAA eligible, yet you own) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 268 Td (compliance for the tools you connect, and government sites are not supported. Pilot with) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 252 Td (one team, keep permissions tight, then expand.) Tj ET
BT /F2 14 Tf 54 222 Td (1. A bridge. Not a dashboard.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 203 Td (The Datadog MCP Server links your observability data to any agent that speaks the Model) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 187 Td (Context Protocol, so you ask instead of clicking through screens.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 54 163 Td (Claims) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 146 Td (• The Datadog MCP Server bridges Datadog observability data to AI agents, so logs,) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 130 Td (metrics, traces, dashboards and monitors can be queried in natural language.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 54 106 Td (Assets and alt text) Tj ET
endstream
